Z||000008||artherd||12-06-2001||02:58 AM||||Aack, you guys must be running crap for tyres!<P>My mildly sticky (the Northstar car is getting even stickier tyres) 215/45/17 dunlop W10s will ONLY lay rubber if the clutch is dumped above 4500+ or so, in first.<P>Otherwise, they just *hold*.<P>Second gear will chirp.  But only in the rain. Never dry. not even if I try and 'power shift' it :S|<P>Third gear? heck no. Third is for going 90mph while merging  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||64.3.146.254||reg||3
